[[2047,127,0,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               controls the heater fan circuit.</p><p>The supply at the relay contact comes from\nthe battery through the line for the A/C maxifuse up to 2/99 or\nof \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99, while the coil energizing is controlled\nby the ignition (INT/A) from the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up\nto 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F6</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from\n2/99.</p><p>The relay \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>J35</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               supplies the control\nknob \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H81</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : this controls the fan at the different speeds through\nthe regulator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The voltage control system varies according\nto the position of the knob and passes or does not pass through\nthe resistors of the regulator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               determining the four different\nvoltage signals for the fan \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N85</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which sends outside or recirculation\nair to the duct/distributor unit at 4 different speeds.</p><p>The regulator \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>O30</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has a thermal contact\nwhich protects against dangerous overvoltages.</p><p>The intake of outside air is controlled\nby the motor \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>N82</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which operates the flap between the two\nextreme positions of &quot;dynamic air&quot; and &quot;recirculation&quot;.</p><p>The activation of the motor is controlled\nby the button located in the controls \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H80</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              : this switch receives\na supply controlled by the ignition (INT/A) from the line protected\nby the fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F6</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p><p>and is connected to earth: when the supply\nand earth are reversed, the motor&#x27;s direction of rotation is reversed.\nWith the recirculation switched on, the LED in the button for \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H80</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               also\ncomes on.</p><p>The controls unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H80</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has ideograms\nwhich are lit up when the side lights are on by means of the line\ncoming from the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B11</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               up to 2/99 or fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional\nfuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               from 2/99.</p>"]]